  <diagram id="03-funding-formula-handoffs" name="03-funding-formula-handoffs" description="An illustration, not a real NHSBSA case: a sequence of seven handoffs between four roles, read from the top down. The four roles run across the top, each with a vertical line below: commissioner, analyst, critical friend, and Analysis Senior Responsible Officer. A dark heading down the left names the phase each handoff falls in. 1, in engagement and scoping: the commissioner passes the analyst the decision, the deadline and how certain the answer has to be. 2, in design: the analyst passes the critical friend the design and plan, with the critical friend named on it. 3, in analysis: the critical friend passes the analyst findings, which are the analyst's to act on. 4, 5, 6 and 7 are all in delivery, communication and sign-off. 4: the analyst passes the commissioner draft results, so they are understood before sign-off. 5: the analyst passes the Analysis Senior Responsible Officer the assurance evidence. 6: the critical friend passes the Analysis Senior Responsible Officer the Lead Assurer sign-off, which comes before the approval. 7: the Analysis Senior Responsible Officer passes the commissioner the approval, as fit for its intended use. The example is a funding allocation formula at Level 4.">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="680" pageHeight="768" math="0" shadow="0" background="#FFFFFF">
